Practical 1 — Creating Simple Application
and Testing Application
A. Using Visual Studio — College PC
Step 1: Open Visual Studio
Start → Visual Studio
Select:
Create a new project
Step 2: Select project
Search:
ASP.NET Core Web App (Model-View-Controller)
Select it → Next
Step 3: Configure project
Project Name: Practical1
Click Next.
Step 4: Additional Information
Select the available .NET version.
Authentication Type: None
Configure for HTTPS: ✓
Docker: No
Click Create. Step 5: Open the View
In Solution Explorer:
Views
↓
Home
↓
Index.cshtml
Replace the contents with:
@{
ViewData["Title"] = "Practical 1";
}
<h1>My First ASP.NET Core MVC Application</h1>
<p>Welcome to my C# practical.</p>
<p>This application is running successfully.</p>
Save:
Ctrl + S
Step 6: Run
Click the green Run ▶ button at the top.
OR:
Ctrl + F5
Step 7: Check Output
The browser opens automatically. Example:
https://localhost:7000
Expected output:
My First ASP.NET Core MVC Application
